    <h2>Flagged for Review</h2>
    <p class="lede">Verification standard used on this site: every table row must link an official source (a .gov site, Covered California, or Kalshi's official help center for Kalshi-specific practice). If a value could not be confirmed from an official source, it is left blank, marked <span class="badge b-unverified">Unverified</span>, and listed here. Inconsistencies between official sources are marked <span class="badge b-flagged">Flagged</span> and listed here too. Nothing on this page blocks anything else on the site.</p>
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="resolved-h">
    <h3 id="resolved-h">Answered in the 2026-10-18 verification pass</h3>
    <div class="panel">
      <ul>
        <li><strong>What added Welf. &amp; Inst. Code &sect;14005.69?</strong> SB 164 (Chapter 27, Statutes of 2026, Sec. 75) added it effective June 29, 2026; AB 2161 (Chapter 209, Statutes of 2026) amended it. The Leginfo history note is the controlling statement: <a href="https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=WIC&amp;sectionNum=14005.69">consolidated section</a>, <a href="https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/billNavClient.xhtml?bill_id=202520260SB164">SB 164</a>. This corrects the earlier attribution of the section to AB 2161. Recorded as CA-31.</li>
        <li><strong>Does the $580 route count unearned income?</strong> Yes. It is measured by MAGI-based income for the MAGI household (42 CFR 435.552; 42 CFR 435.603), which includes net rental income, interest, and net capital gains &mdash; so $0 earned income is not a bar. Only the county&rsquo;s month-by-month documentation method for trading gains stays open. Recorded as FL-17.</li>
        <li><strong>Who is excluded?</strong> The exclusion list comes from SB 164, amended by AB 2161; the &ldquo;23&rdquo; figure on this site is a count of this project&rsquo;s catalogue of exemption, deemed-compliance, and hardship rows, not an official enumeration. Recorded as OP-9.</li>
        <li><strong>Do the subdivision letters in the code display match the statute?</strong> No &mdash; the Leginfo display still shows the SB 164 text (through subdivision (n)), while AB 2161 is the operative amending act (through subdivision (r)). The mismatch is a display lag, confirmed by reading the chaptered AB 2161 text in full; every statutory citation on this site now follows AB 2161 and names it. Recorded as FL-28.</li>
        <li><strong>Citizen vs. green card.</strong> Added on request: U.S. citizens keep full Medi-Cal with no premium; LPRs inside the five-year wait move to fee-for-service in January 2027, with a later July 2027 premium step for ages 21&ndash;59 who are not pregnant. <a href="https://www.dhcs.ca.gov/immigration-status-and-changes-to-medi-cal-eligibility/">DHCS immigration-status table</a>. Recorded as MC-19.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

