  <section aria-labelledby="next-h">
    <h3 id="next-h">What to do with these</h3>
    <div class="panel">
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Tax character of Kalshi event contracts</strong> &mdash; take the contract facts (P&amp;L statements, trade exports) to a CPA or tax attorney before filing; the IRS has not ruled.</li>
        <li><strong>Work-rule specifics ($580 standard, trading hours)</strong> &mdash; ask your county Medi-Cal office in writing, and keep the answer. Two protections are independently documented: counties must check every other basis of eligibility before denying or terminating, and existing members have 30 calendar days plus two contact attempts before noncompliance is found (<a href="https://www.dhcs.ca.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/25-30.pdf">ACWDL 25-30</a>). The data-conflict duty itself is real and sits at WIC &sect;14005.69(i) of the AB 2161 chaptered text, which also says the county must let you confirm the information before any adverse action; the code display on Leginfo still shows the earlier SB 164 wording, so cite the chaptered bill when quoting a subdivision.</li>
        <li><strong>Official-page wording differences</strong> &mdash; linked side by side above for manual comparison; the operative county instruction (MEDIL I26-25) is the most specific California document.</li>
        <li><strong>2027 poverty guidelines</strong> &mdash; republish around January 2027; thresholds on this site will need a refresh for the 2028 coverage year.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
